From f5a83d2f11d5389a94bc61d8e210532ed7100dc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:01:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): create_overlap compares targets, not only title
 words [daveey]

Overlap audit t_01a189c70884fa59 (MacBook + mini, 24 h) and its hub leg
(t_01a189b2d186a986): 12 of 16 refusal groups (108 attempts) were false.
Every logged why was "titles share N words (...)" on boilerplate while
the cards named different targets.

Problem: kanban_create refused e.g. "daveey-mini: gateway 45464 may run
stale hermes-mods plugins" against MacBook "David-MBP: gateway 81967 ..."
(7 retries), "BB-1155 ... mini ... disk" against "BB-1197, BB-1202,
BB-1205 ... metta3 ... disk" (85 retries), the mini probe leg against
the MacBook leg, "daveey/hermes-mods" red CI against "daveey/hermes"
green CI, and a waiter against the producer it parks on.
Why 1: _reasons matches on shared title words (>=3, >=50%) alone.
  Evidence: logged why lines name only the shared words.
Why 2: nothing compares which machine/process/ticket/repo each title
  names; those tokens are what differ in every false pair.
Root (happened): the match decision has no notion of target identity.
Root (not caught): the regression fixtures only covered board-slug
  references (004623277d, e4180d7535), no same-template/different-target
  pairs and no cross-gateway pairs.

Fix: distinct_target() vetoes a match when both titles name a target in
one class and the sets are disjoint: repo (owner/repo; a title with none
uses its body's single repo), host (MacBook/MBP/David-MBP, mini/
daveey-mini, hermes-hub, metta<N>, ...), process (gateway|pid <n>),
ticket (ABC-123, #123 but not run/job #n). A differing sha alone never
vetoes (a newer revision of the same check is the same owner's work);
it does only when one title inverts the other's check (removal vs not).
Same target stays refused, remote-owned too: no gateway exemption.
waits_on(): a create that parks/waits on a card or names it producer/
parent is not its duplicate.

Also: under a HERMES_KANBAN_DB pin every board slug resolves to the
pinned file, so one card came back once per board, labelled with each
board's slug (hub 10-30 08:04:58Z, 12:05:05Z, 7x). Read each resolved
file once under the board that owns it; the pin itself is unchanged.

Case 5 ("Fix remaining Inbox poster conformance", 10-29 17:54 PDT):
replaying the exact create over each kanban_overlap.py revision gives
the exact 7 matches on d0cc66e9f4..004623277d and none from e4180d7535;
the creating session started 16:25:11 PDT, before the MacBook applied
e4180d7535 at 16:29:43. Stale caller, already fixed in source; its
fixture passes on base and pins that.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_url_slug.py, real titles
and bodies from the audit evidence; 21 fail on base, all pass; true
duplicate controls (PR181, v12 round, drain capability owner, same
host/pid, same incident, same repo, same/newer-sha check) pass on both.
